// The metaprogramming effects: the compiler operations library code running
// inside the compiler may perform. Reading the program needs no Meta effect,
// so a read-only lint's row is `-[]>`; a marker or derive that writes checked
// declarations is `-[Meta.Generate]>`, and replacing a declaration's body is
// `Meta.Rewrite`. Adding a type from text checks `Generate`, `Types` and `Raw`
// together. The bare `#FX` lists no machine effect: host work keeps its own
// machine effects and gates.
// The form is that of Compiler/Prelude/Effects.jet, and
// Tools/agent/CoreSourceRows.jet reads it into the compiler after
// Core/Effects/Effects.jet.
#FX
Meta: enum {
    Generate
    Include
    Rewrite
    Types
    Raw

    impl Effect {}
}
